    "title": "Canadian truck driver dies in rollover crash in Grant County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Grace Samels ,\n9 hours ago\nGRANT COUNTY, Ind. (WANE) -- A semi-truck driver from Canada has died after veering off I-69 and crashing.\nAccording to the Indiana State Police, 60-year-old Lee Lauzon from Ontario, Canada, was traveling south on I-69 near the 269-mile marker in Washington Township, Indiana. Preliminary investigation showed that Lauzon had veered off the side of the highway for an unknown reason and rolled before coming to a stop.\nWhen police and medics arrived, Lauzon was pronounced dead at the scene. Investigators have determined that Lauzon had not been under the influence of drugs or alcohol.\nThis crash remains under investigation.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.\nAdd to Preferred Sources\n4",
    "summary": "(WANE) -- A semi-truck driver from Canada has died after veering off I-69 and crashing. Preliminary investigation showed that Lauzon had veered off the side of the highway for an unknown reason and rolled before coming to a stop. When police and medics arrived, Lauzon was pronounced dead at the scene. Investigators have determined that Lauzon had not been under the influence of drugs or alcohol. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
